"""Original lymphoid chapter: eight acute lymphoblastic leukemia questions."""
from qbank_authoring import question,ref,finalize
AL=ref('NCI: Adult Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia Treatment—Health Professional PDQ','https://www.cancer.gov/types/leukemia/hp/adult-all-treatment-pdq')
rows=[]
def q(*a,**k):rows.append(question(*a,**k))
q('Marrow blasts express TdT, CD19 and cytoplasmic CD79a but lack myeloperoxidase. Which lineage is best supported?', 'Precursor B lymphoid',[
 ('Mature plasma cell','TdT and the precursor phenotype argue against a mature plasma-cell process.'),('Myeloid','The stated B-lineage pattern and absent MPO favor precursor B disease.'),('Mature T lymphoid','The markers do not support that lineage.')],
 'Lineage assignment requires a coherent marker pattern', '**TdT supports immaturity and B-lineage markers identify the relevant differentiation.**',['No single nonspecific marker should be used alone.','Mixed-phenotype disease requires formal lineage criteria.'], '**Complete the genetic and clinical classification.**',['BCR::ABL1 and other alterations affect treatment.','Assess CNS and other sites under the ALL pathway.'],[['Immaturity','TdT'],['B lineage','CD19 and cytoplasmic CD79a'],['Myeloid evidence','MPO absent in the stated pattern']],[AL])
q('An adolescent has a bulky anterior mediastinal mass and blasts with cytoplasmic CD3 and TdT. Which diagnosis is most likely?', 'T-lymphoblastic leukemia/lymphoma',[
 ('CLL','This is a mature B-cell disorder and does not fit the blast phenotype.'),('Plasma-cell myeloma','The phenotype and age-related presentation differ.'),('Classical Hodgkin lymphoma established by mass location alone','The precursor T-cell phenotype identifies a different disease.')],
 'A thymic-region mass can accompany precursor T-cell disease', '**Cytoplasmic CD3 is strong T-lineage evidence.**',['The leukemia-versus-lymphoma designation depends on the disease distribution and marrow involvement framework.','Airway and venous compression can create immediate risk.'], '**Obtain safe diagnostic material and stage appropriately.**',['Plan anesthesia carefully with a mediastinal mass.','Treatment uses a lymphoblastic rather than a generic mature-lymphoma strategy.'],[['Location','Anterior mediastinum'],['Phenotype','TdT and cytoplasmic CD3'],['Care','Urgent risk and ALL-type pathway']],[AL],style='clinical_scenario')
q('Why is BCR::ABL1 testing important in newly diagnosed adult B-ALL?', 'A positive result identifies a targetable kinase-driven subtype requiring an appropriate TKI-containing strategy',[
 ('It proves the disease is always chronic-phase CML','The lesion can occur in acute lymphoblastic disease.'),('It eliminates any need for CNS-directed therapy','Sanctuary-site management remains relevant.'),('It means all chemotherapy and immunotherapy choices are identical to BCR::ABL1-negative ALL','The molecular subtype changes planning.')],
 'The same fusion can occur in different clinical disease contexts', '**Philadelphia-positive ALL has a specific targeted-treatment pathway.**',['Distinguish de novo ALL from a CML lymphoid blast-phase presentation where relevant.','Transcript and MRD monitoring need an appropriate baseline.'], '**Select the current combination according to fitness and protocol.**',['TKI choice, immune-based therapy and transplant decisions are individualized.','Do not treat a fusion result in isolation from the full diagnosis.'],[['Biomarker','BCR::ABL1'],['Consequence','TKI-containing treatment'],['Other care','MRD and CNS strategy remain important']],[AL])
q('Why is CNS-directed treatment or prophylaxis part of ALL therapy even when initial CSF studies are negative?', 'The CNS is a sanctuary site and systemic marrow control alone does not reliably prevent CNS relapse',[
 ('A negative initial CSF guarantees lifelong absence of CNS disease','It does not eliminate later risk.'),('Intrathecal treatment is merely analgesic','Its purpose is antileukemic.'),('CNS-directed care replaces systemic therapy','Both compartments need appropriate control.')],
 'Control of visible marrow disease is not the entire treatment objective', '**Intrathecal and selected systemic CNS-penetrating therapy address sanctuary risk.**',['The exact programme depends on disease and protocol.','Radiation is selective rather than mandatory for every patient.'], '**Plan procedural timing safely.**',['Review platelet count and coagulation before lumbar puncture.','Avoid delaying urgent systemic care solely to complete an unsafe initial procedure.'],[['Systemic therapy','Marrow and systemic disease'],['CNS-directed therapy','Sanctuary protection'],['Programme','Risk- and protocol-specific']],[AL])
q('Persistent MRD after induction in ALL most appropriately indicates what?', 'A higher relapse risk that can change subsequent treatment planning',[
 ('Guaranteed permanent cure','Residual disease suggests the opposite concern.'),('A result that never affects treatment','MRD is an important response measure.'),('That the initial lineage diagnosis must be incorrect','Persistence does not itself invalidate the original diagnosis.')],
 'Depth of response is a major component of ALL risk assessment', '**MRD detects disease below routine morphology.**',['Assay, sensitivity and time point matter.','The original phenotype or molecular marker supports tracking.'], '**Use the result within the treatment protocol.**',['Selected patients may need immune therapy, intensification or transplant assessment.','A negative result reduces risk but does not guarantee cure.'],[['MRD positive','Residual burden and higher risk'],['MRD negative','Deeper response with assay limits'],['Decision','Protocol-based adaptation']],[AL])
q('What is the mechanism of blinatumomab?', 'A bispecific construct linking CD19-positive B cells to CD3-positive T cells',[
 ('A CD22-directed antibody-drug conjugate','That describes inotuzumab ozogamicin.'),('A BCL2 inhibitor','That describes venetoclax.'),('An ATP-site ABL inhibitor','That describes a TKI mechanism.')],
 'A bispecific therapy recruits T cells to the malignant B-cell target', '**CD19 and CD3 binding creates a cytotoxic immune interaction.**',['It has roles in specific B-ALL treatment settings.','Target expression and prior treatment affect suitability.'], '**Monitor immune-activation toxicity.**',['Cytokine-release syndrome and neurological effects are important.','Use protocol-defined observation, interruption and treatment measures.'],[['Target cell','CD19-positive B cell'],['Effector','CD3-positive T cell'],['Safety','CRS and neurological toxicity']],[AL])
q('Inotuzumab ozogamicin is associated with which particularly important risk when planning subsequent transplantation?', 'Hepatic sinusoidal obstruction syndrome',[
 ('A complete absence of hepatic toxicity','A major hepatic risk is recognized.'),('Permanent protection from all infections','Immunosuppressive and marrow effects remain relevant.'),('Mandatory pulmonary fibrosis in every patient','That is not the defining universal risk.')],
 'A targeted antibody-drug conjugate can affect later treatment safety', '**Inotuzumab targets CD22 and delivers a cytotoxic payload.**',['Hepatic sinusoidal injury is an important complication.','Risk can be influenced by exposure and transplant conditioning.'], '**Coordinate the treatment sequence early.**',['Review liver function and cumulative risk.','Balance disease control against transplant-related harm.'],[['Target','CD22'],['Class','Antibody-drug conjugate'],['Key concern','Sinusoidal obstruction syndrome']],[AL])
q('A patient develops fever, hypotension and hypoxemia soon after CD19-directed cellular therapy. Which syndrome is a major concern while evaluating infection?', 'Cytokine-release syndrome',[
 ('Tumor lysis established solely from fever','TLS requires the relevant metabolic assessment.'),('A harmless expected fever needing no review','Circulatory and respiratory compromise requires urgent care.'),('Acute iron deficiency as the explanation','That does not fit the temporal inflammatory syndrome.')],
 'Immune-effector activation can cause systemic inflammatory toxicity', '**CRS can include fever with escalating circulatory or respiratory support needs.**',['Infection can coexist and must be assessed.','Neurological toxicity is related but assessed separately.'], '**Use the cellular-therapy grading and treatment protocol.**',['Support organs and use indicated immune-directed treatment.','Do not assume every post-treatment deterioration is a single mechanism.'],[['CRS','Systemic inflammatory syndrome'],['Parallel differential','Infection and other treatment complications'],['Management','Protocol-based urgent support']],[AL],style='clinical_scenario')
